module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_width_constrained_integer_admits_a_value_outside_its_width

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_width_constrained_integer_admits_a_value_outside_its_width: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_width_constrained_integer_admits_a_value_outside_its_width" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value typed by a width-constrained integer (std.integer UInt8..UInt128, Int8..Int128: Compose<carrier, MachineWidth<N>>) that is not in [0, 2^N) (unsigned) or [-2^(N-1), 2^(N-1)) (signed). HARM: silent wrongness at the declared type -- a literal 300 at UInt8, or 255 + 1 typed UInt8, is accepted and evaluated as an ordinary Int, so the interpreted and emitted realizations of one program disagree and nothing said the width was crossed. OPERATOR RULING (CHECKED): a width is a checked refinement on Int, wrapping exists only as a named operation, and there is no implicit narrowing or widening. This row is the width-specific face of bounded_natural_arithmetic_evaluated_as_unbounded_int, which keeps the arithmetic history; it is separate because the literal boundary, the arithmetic boundary and the carrier boundary climb on different triggers.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: Compose is a Phantom and transparent to Int at a formal, so no check at a call or return consults N; the class is not an overflow of the host Int (that refuses) but a missing refusal at the DECLARED width. THREE BOUNDARIES, kept apart because a rung is the minimum across them: (1) LITERAL -- an Int literal at a width position; (2) ARITHMETIC -- infix + - * on a width operand and the word32_* family that routes it; (3) CARRIER -- a non-literal Int reaching a width formal or field.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent wrongness) on all three boundaries. RUNG NOW, BOUNDARY (1) ONLY (A0-2): a located, typed refusal at infer -- v2.compiler.infer infer_int_literal_value_at reads Compose<A, MachineWidth<N>> and refuses a literal outside std.machine_width_range machine_width_admits with infer_reason_literal_outside_machine_width -- mitigation by a refusal that is loud and located, not construction, because a non-literal Int still reaches the same formal unchecked. Boundaries (2) and (3) are unchanged. SUBJECT GRAIN OF THE EVIDENCE: the executed claims assemble peers that restate std.integer's Int, UInt, UInt8 and Int8 declarations as it writes them, NOT the real std.integer module (28 modules in its import closure); the rung is therefore established for that declared shape, and the real-module assembly is the next evidence trigger, at capability grain: A CLAIM HARNESS THAT ASSEMBLES THE REAL std.integer CLOSURE WITHIN A CLAIM'S STEP BUDGET.",
    "CEILING, WITH REASON: structurally impossible at the carrier -- a sole-constructed bounded-natural carrier (std.bounded_nat is the operation family; the newtype with sole_constructor is the carrier) whose range admission is its only mint, so an out-of-width value has no constructor. Decidable and fully modeled, hence reachable; not undecidable, so not a ratchet.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, AT CAPABILITY GRAIN: (2) the word32_* operations and sha1/sha2 consume std.bounded_nat's declared arithmetic, SUFFICIENT FOR no infix arithmetic on a width operand to remain on the interpreted route; (3) a width carrier with sole construction exists and the Compose sole_constructor handling in the infer lane admits its mint, SUFFICIENT FOR a non-literal Int to be refused at a width formal. The discriminating controls are width_literal_admission: 300 at UInt8 refuses, 255 at UInt8 is admitted.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.machine_width_range", decl_name: "machine_width_admits", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.width_literal_admission", decl_name: "wla_uint8_300_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.width_literal_admission", decl_name: "wla_uint8_255_is_admitted", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
